<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
      SummaFlow footer - compact wide editorial composition.

      Source-controlled and self-applying: inherits website.layout and replaces
      BOTH footer nodes, at high priority so this definition wins on import
      without any manual Website Builder step.

        1. //div[@id='footer']                   -> the SummaFlow footer panel
        2. //div[hasclass('o_footer_copyright')] -> the single SummaFlow legal row

      (2) is why an earlier iteration still showed a legacy
      "Copyright (c) SummaFlow" strip: in website.layout the copyright block is
      a SIBLING of #footer inside <footer id="bottom">, not a child of it, so
      replacing #footer alone left it rendering underneath. It is replaced
      structurally rather than hidden with CSS.

      Composition (ONE four-column grid, then the brand signature):

        col 1   brand wordmark + Sign In / Request a Free Trial + contact metadata + socials
        col 2   SOLUTIONS (Platform, Resources)
        col 3   EXPLORE (Company, Security)
        col 4   STAY UPDATED: copy, form, inline success,
                EXPLORE AI SUMMARY
        then    oversized SummaFlow wordmark, full-bleed, nearly full width

      The earlier separate middle utility row (contact left / AI centre /
      socials far right) is gone on client instruction: it read as two
      unrelated footers stacked. Its three blocks now live inside the columns
      above, each exactly once — no duplicate copies left behind.

      Both divs keep t-ignore="true" so the Website Builder never treats this
      footer as editable content and never persists a divergent copy into the
      database arch.

      The Odoo newsletter form (s_newsletter_subscribe_form / js_subscribe /
      data-list-id="1", plus the js_subscribed_wrap success node) is preserved
      verbatim so its real subscribe behaviour keeps working; only its
      presentation and state styling change.

      CTA controls are plain anchors carrying the header's button language
      (.sf-button plus the primary / secondary modifier, styled in _footer.scss
      from the live header's Bootstrap .btn values). The earlier gradient
      fill was removed on client instruction: no gradient, no animated fill, no
      extra span, and no JavaScript. Non-void elements are written with
      explicit closing tags on purpose: a self-closed <span/> would be parsed
      by HTML as an open tag and would swallow its siblings.
    -->
    <template id="summaflow_footer" inherit_id="website.layout"
              name="SummaFlow Footer" priority="99">

        <!-- 1. Main footer panel -->
        <xpath expr="//div[@id='footer']" position="replace">
            <div id="footer" t-ignore="true" t-if="not no_footer" class="sf-footer">
                <div class="sf-footer__panel">

                    <!-- Row 1: brand lead, two nav groups, newsletter -->
                    <div class="sf-footer__top">
                        <div class="sf-footer__lead">
                            <div class="sf-footer__logotype">SummaFlow</div>
                            <div class="sf-footer__ctas">
                                <a class="sf-button sf-button--primary"
                                   href="https://app.summaflow.com/login"
                                   target="_blank"
                                   rel="noopener noreferrer">
                                    Sign In
                                </a>
                                <a class="sf-button sf-button--secondary"
                                   href="/contactus">
                                    Request a Free Trial
                                </a>
                            </div>

                            <!--
                              Contact details belong to the brand column, not to
                              a separate utility row: they read as metadata
                              under the two CTAs, in smaller muted type, with no
                              decorative icon chips.
                            -->
                            <div class="sf-footer__details">
                                <ul class="sf-footer__contact">
                                    <li><a href="mailto:info@summaflow.com">info@summaflow.com</a></li>
                                    <li>
                                        <span class="sf-footer__contact-key">WhatsApp</span>
                                        <!--
                                          wa.me, not tel: - this is the
                                          WhatsApp number, so the link must
                                          open a WhatsApp chat instead of
                                          placing a phone call. Displayed
                                          number unchanged; wa.me needs the
                                          international form with no + or
                                          spaces.
                                        -->
                                        <a href="https://wa.me/85292209701"
                                           target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                                           aria-label="Chat with SummaFlow on WhatsApp"><span class="o_force_ltr">+852 9220 9701</span></a>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                                <p class="sf-footer__address">GF, Koon Nam House, 12-14 Shing Wong Street, Hong Kong</p>
                            </div>

                            <!--
                              Socials belong to the brand block, under the
                              contact metadata. Icons only, monochrome, no text
                              labels and no background chips; the network names
                              are carried by aria-label/title. The three hrefs
                              are the ones already in the arch - placeholders
                              the client still has to supply.
                            -->
                            <ul class="sf-footer__social">
                                <li>
                                    <a href="https://www.twitter.com/your-page" target="_blank"
                                       rel="noopener" title="X" aria-label="SummaFlow on X">
                                        <i class="fa fa-twitter" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </a>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/your-page" target="_blank"
                                       rel="noopener" title="LinkedIn" aria-label="SummaFlow on LinkedIn">
                                        <i class="fa fa-linkedin" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </a>
                                </li>
                                <li>
                                    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/your-page" target="_blank"
                                       rel="noopener" title="YouTube" aria-label="SummaFlow on YouTube">
                                        <i class="fa fa-youtube-play" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </a>
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>

                        <!--
                          Navigation groups, regrouped on client instruction:
                          SOLUTIONS (Platform, Resources) and EXPLORE (Company,
                          Security). Vertical stacked lists, one link per row -
                          never two links side by side. Routes are unchanged.
                        -->
                        <nav class="sf-footer__navgroup" aria-label="Solutions">
                            <div class="sf-footer__head">Solutions</div>
                            <ul class="sf-footer__list">
                                <li><a href="/platform">Platform</a></li>
                                <li><a href="/blog">Resources</a></li>
                            </ul>
                        </nav>

                        <nav class="sf-footer__navgroup" aria-label="Explore">
                            <div class="sf-footer__head">Explore</div>
                            <ul class="sf-footer__list">
                                <li><a href="/company">Company</a></li>
                                <li><a href="/security">Security</a></li>
                            </ul>
                        </nav>

                        <div class="sf-footer__news">
                            <div class="sf-footer__head">Stay updated</div>
                            <p class="sf-footer__news-copy">A weekly roundup of news and insights on the world of LLMs.</p>
                            <div data-vxml="001" data-name="Newsletter"
                                 class="s_newsletter_subscribe_form s_newsletter_list js_subscribe sf-footer__form"
                                 data-snippet="s_newsletter_subscribe_form" data-list-id="1">
                                <!-- Form first, success state DIRECTLY BELOW it:
                                     Odoo only toggles d-none on these two
                                     wrappers, so document order is what decides
                                     where the confirmation appears. -->
                                <div class="js_subscribe_wrap">
                                    <div class="input-group sf-footer__field">
                                        <input type="email" name="email" aria-label="Email address"
                                               placeholder="Email address"
                                               class="s_newsletter_subscribe_form_input js_subscribe_value form-control"/>
                                        <a role="button" href="#"
                                           class="js_subscribe_btn o_submit o_translate_inline btn sf-button sf-button--primary">
                                            Subscribe
                                        </a>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="js_subscribed_wrap d-none sf-footer__news-done">
                                    <p>
                                        <i class="fa fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                        <span>Thanks for registering.</span>
                                    </p>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                        <!--
                          Explore AI Summary: the four AI assistants a summary can
                          be opened in. Marks are the official monochrome brand
                          glyphs, stored locally under static/src/icons/ai/ and
                          served from the module (no CDN, no remote URL). Icons
                          only: provider names are carried by alt/title.
                        -->
                        <div class="sf-footer__ai">
                            <div class="sf-footer__head">Explore AI Summary</div>
                            <t t-set="sf_ai_class" t-value="'sf-footer__ai-marks'"/>
                            <t t-set="sf_ai_size" t-value="22"/>
                            <t t-call="website_summaflow.ai_marks"/>
                        </div>

                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!--
                      Row 3: the oversized brand signature.

                      Deliberately plain HTML text, NOT SVG. The previous SVG
                      version relied on `fill: url(#sf_footer_wordmark)` coming
                      from the compiled stylesheet; Odoo's asset bundler
                      rewrites url() references inside CSS, which can break a
                      bare in-document fragment reference and leave the glyphs
                      unpainted. This treatment uses background-image +
                      background-clip:text, with the gradient declared directly
                      on the element, and is sized in vw so the word tracks the
                      full panel width at every viewport.
                    -->
                    <div class="sf-footer__signature" aria-hidden="true">SummaFlow</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </xpath>

        <!-- 2. The ONE legal row; structurally replaces Odoo's copyright block
             (which also carries web.brand_promotion) so no legacy strip can
             render below the SummaFlow footer. -->
        <xpath expr="//div[hasclass('o_footer_copyright')]" position="replace">
            <div id="o_footer_copyright" t-ignore="true" t-if="not no_footer"
                 class="o_footer_copyright sf-footer__legal">
                <div class="sf-footer__legal-inner">
                    <span class="sf-footer__legal-copy">&#169; 2026 SummaFlow</span>
                    <nav class="sf-footer__legal-nav" aria-label="Legal">
                        <a href="/support">Support</a>
                        <a href="/oauth-verification">Verification</a>
                        <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy</a>
                        <a href="/terms-and-conditions">Terms</a>
                    </nav>
                </div>
            </div>
        </xpath>
    </template>
</odoo>
